 ### Fixed

+- `OrchestratorHooks.afterModelResponse` now receives the summed `UsageMetadata` across every provider call in the turn (`totalUsage`), rather than only the final round's usage. Previously, each round overwrote the recorded usage with `lastUsage = outcome.usage ?? lastUsage`, so any turn that executed tools under-counted input, output, and total tokens by every earlier round's usage. Rounds that report no usage are skipped without zeroing earlier rounds, and a turn in which no round reports usage still passes `undefined`. **Migration note**: the third parameter of `afterModelResponse(session, responseText, totalUsage)` is now the turn total (`inputTokens`, `outputTokens`, `totalTokens` summed across all rounds that reported usage) instead of the final round's usage; single-round turns with no tool calls are unchanged.
 - `onError` and `afterSession` hooks now fire when `beforeSession` throws, matching the guarantee the hook names imply. Previously, a throw from `beforeSession` escaped the `try`/`finally` block entirely, so neither hook ran. **Migration note**: if your `afterSession` hook assumed it would only be called after a full session turn, it will now also be called when `beforeSession` itself fails — the hook can inspect the session to detect this case (no entries beyond the initial user message will have been processed).

